---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
const APP = "https://login.ollastack.com";

const sections = [
  { id: "why", title: "How it works" },
  { id: "enable", title: "Enable uploads" },
  { id: "flow", title: "The upload flow" },
  { id: "link", title: "Linking to a submission" },
  { id: "manage", title: "List + delete" },
];
---

<Base current="docs" title="Docs — File uploads — Ollastack">
  <div class="docs-shell container-wide">
    <aside class="sidebar">
      <div class="side-eyebrow mono">/ docs / uploads</div>
      <nav>
        <ul>
          {sections.map((s) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </nav>
      <div class="side-back"><a href="/docs">← Back to docs</a></div>
    </aside>

    <article class="content">
      <span class="chip mono"><span class="dot"></span>file uploads</span>
      <h1 class="display">Accept files without a storage backend.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Uploads go straight from the browser to object storage with a presigned
        URL — the bytes never transit our API — and link themselves to the
        submission. You add an upload field; we handle the storage.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why">How it works</h2>
      <p>
        A <code>file</code> field on a form is backed by a three-step presigned
        flow. The client asks for a short-lived upload URL, PUTs the file directly
        to storage, confirms it, then references the upload id in the submission.
        The file is validated against the form's limits (size, MIME type) before
        the URL is ever issued.
      </p>

      <h2 id="enable">Enable uploads</h2>
      <p>
        Add a <code>file</code> field in the builder and set the per-form limits
        (max size, max files, allowed MIME types). Object storage must be enabled
        on the server — the presign call returns <code>503</code> if it isn't.
      </p>

      <h2 id="flow">The upload flow</h2>
      <p><strong>1. Ask for a presigned URL.</strong></p>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X POST {APP}/api/forms/<span class="hl">&lt;formId&gt;</span>/uploads \
     -H <span class="s">"Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;"</span> -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/json"</span> \
     -d <span class="s">'&#123; "fieldId": "resume", "filename": "cv.pdf", "mimeType": "application/pdf", "sizeBytes": 84211 &#125;'</span>
<span class="ok">{`{"uploadId": "...", "uploadUrl": "https://...", "storageKey": "...", "expiresAt": "..."}`}</span></pre>
      <p><strong>2. PUT the bytes</strong> straight to <code>uploadUrl</code> (not to our API).</p>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X PUT <span class="s">"&lt;uploadUrl&gt;"</span> --data-binary @cv.pdf -H <span class="s">"Content-Type: application/pdf"</span></pre>
      <p><strong>3. Confirm</strong> the upload completed.</p>
      <pre class="code"><span class="prompt">$</span> <span class="k">curl</span> -X POST {APP}/api/forms/<span class="hl">&lt;formId&gt;</span>/uploads/<span class="hl">&lt;uploadId&gt;</span>/confirm \
     -H <span class="s">"Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;"</span></pre>

      <h2 id="link">Linking to a submission</h2>
      <p>
        Include the upload ids in the submission payload (e.g. an
        <code>uploadIds</code> array). When the submission is stored, those
        uploads are automatically attached to it, so they show up alongside the
        lead in the inbox and aren't garbage-collected as orphans.
      </p>

      <h2 id="manage">List + delete</h2>
      <p>
        <code>GET /api/forms/&#123;formId&#125;/uploads</code> lists a form's uploads;
        <code>DELETE /api/forms/&#123;formId&#125;/uploads/&#123;uploadId&#125;</code> removes
        one (and its stored object). Both need the <code>forms:read</code> /
        <code>forms:write</code> scope respectively.
      </p>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" href={`${APP}/dashboard`}>Open the dashboard</a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost btn-lg" href="/docs">Back to docs</a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .docs-shell { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr; gap: 56px; padding: 64px 28px 96px; }
  .sidebar { position: sticky; top: 80px; align-self: start; }
  .side-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.08em; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .sidebar nav ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
  .sidebar nav a { display: block; padding: 6px 10px; border-radius: 6px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  .sidebar nav a:hover { background: var(--bg-sunken); color: var(--ink); }
  .side-back { margin-top: 24px; font-size: 13px; }
  .side-back a { color: var(--muted); }
  .content { max-width: 760px; }
  .chip { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 3px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 999px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted); margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .chip .dot { width: 6px; height: 6px; background: var(--accent); border-radius: 50%; }
  .content h1 { font-size: 44px; margin: 0 0 14px; letter-spacing: -0.02em; line-height: 1.05; }
  .content h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 48px 0 12px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; scroll-margin-top: 80px; }
  .content .lede { font-size: 18px; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 620px; }
  .content p { line-height: 1.7; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content ul { line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 22px; margin: 0 0 14px; }
  .content code { background: var(--bg-sunken); border: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 0 5px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.9em; }
  .code { background: var(--code-bg); color: var(--code-fg); border-radius: 12px; padding: 18px 22px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.7; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; margin: 8px 0 14px; }
  .code .prompt { color: var(--code-prompt); margin-right: 8px; }
  .code .k { color: var(--code-cmd); font-weight: 600; }
  .code .s { color: var(--code-str); }
  .code .hl { color: var(--accent); }
  .code .ok { color: var(--code-ok); display: inline-block; margin-top: 8px; }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: 12px; margin-top: 40px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  @media (max-width: 900px) { .docs-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .sidebar { position: static; } }
</style>
